ummary":"Round 9 (hand-back band) review of FEATURE tb-convergence-sweep-records at head 698bff4. Base and target are both a6f2e8a. The history has gaps, so I assessed the whole feature again rather than assuming earlier rounds passed. Since round 8 (head 94d1183) the only material change I found is in cli/test/sweep-records.test.js. The R1 command-path test now runs six invalid-claim cases through both review.execute and gate.execute: missing disposition, unknown disposition, fixed without a sweep, disputed with a sweep, unknown claim key, and a missing sweep.search. Each case asserts the refusal message, and the test then asserts that no reviewer launched and no result was recorded. Receipt 0, run on 698bff4, shows this test and all 58 focused tests passing. This resolves codex/R1-command-path-cases. The protocol modules have the same line counts as at round 8, and I found no new code defect. The two earlier lows are still there and do not block: CR8-1, an edge case in the review-findings.js prepass, and EV8-1, missing local receipts for current-cli.test.js and gatereeve-cli.test.js. Caveats: hosted CI has not run on this head. It is the planned step after convergence and is not counted here as a success. That only the test file changed since round 8 is the implementer's claim; I checked it with line counts and spot reads, not a byte diff."}]}